# Everything the build does not read. Without this the whole working tree is
# sent to the daemon as context, which on a repository with build output and an
# IDE directory is most of it.

.git
.github
.idea
**/target
docs
*.md
!README.md
cp.txt
compose.yaml
logs

# The interface, which Dockerfile.one builds from source in this same context.
# Its installed dependency tree and its last local build are megabytes the
# daemon would copy and the build would then overwrite anyway - `npm ci` in the
# build stage installs from the lockfile, and `npm run build` writes dist/.
#
# Note what is deliberately *not* excluded: orknux-ui/src/docs/*.md. The manual
# is imported by the bundle rather than fetched, so the interface loses its
# documentation if those are dropped. The `*.md` rule above matches only the top
# level - a pattern in a .dockerignore does not cross a slash - so they survive
# it, and this comment exists so the next person to widen that rule to `**/*.md`
# finds out here rather than from an empty /docs page.
orknux-ui/node_modules
orknux-ui/dist
orknux-ui/*.tsbuildinfo
